#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:1
msgid "Line Filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:3
msgid ""
"For wide wavelength coverage (or many segments), using the full line list"
" in every segment is expensive. PySME provides dynamic line filtering to "
"keep only relevant lines per segment (see [Jian et al. "
"(2026)](https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2026arXiv260504007J/abstract))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:7
msgid "Core Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:9
msgid ""
"Use `linelist_mode` and `line_select_method` together in synthesis or "
"solve:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:11
msgid "`\"all\"`: use all lines (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:12
msgid ""
"`\"dynamic\"`: filter lines by precomputed line properties (recommended "
"for long spectra)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:13
msgid "`\"auto\"`: legacy alias of `\"dynamic\"` (deprecated)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:14
msgid "`line_select_method=\"internal\"`: no external preselection metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:15
msgid "`line_select_method=\"cdr\"`: use `central_depth` + `line_range_*`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:16
msgid "`line_select_method=\"almax\"`: use `almax_ratio` + `line_range_*`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:18
msgid "How Dynamic Filtering Works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:20
msgid "When `linelist_mode=\"dynamic\"`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:22
msgid "PySME ensures line metadata exists for the selected method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:23
msgid "`cdr`: `central_depth`, `line_range_s`, `line_range_e`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:24
msgid "`almax`: `almax_ratio`, `line_range_s`, `line_range_e`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:25
msgid "If metadata is missing or stale, PySME updates it automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:26
msgid ""
"For each segment, PySME keeps lines that overlap the segment range (with "
"broadening margin) and pass a strength threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:28
msgid "Only this reduced line subset is sent to SMElib for that segment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:30
msgid "This can significantly reduce runtime for long or segmented spectra."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:32
msgid "Main Controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:34
msgid "Shared controls:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:35
msgid "`sme.line_select_method`: `internal | cdr | almax`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:36
msgid "`sme.line_select_parallel`: enable/disable parallel metadata update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:37
msgid "`sme.line_select_n_jobs`: number of worker processes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:38
msgid "`sme.line_select_chunk_size`: chunk size for metadata update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:39
msgid "`sme.line_select_recompute`: `if_stale | always | never`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:40
msgid "`sme.line_select_stale_thres`: stale thresholds for model changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:41
msgid "CDR method controls:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:42
msgid "`sme.line_select_cdr_strength_thres`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:43
msgid "`sme.line_select_cdr_bin_width`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:44
msgid "`line_precompute_database` / `cdr_create` (function args)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:45
msgid "ALMAX method controls:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:46
msgid "`sme.line_select_almax_threshold`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:47
msgid "`sme.line_select_almax_use_bins`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:48
msgid "`sme.line_select_almax_bin_width`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:50
msgid ""
"`line_precompute_database` is a shared on-disk cache for both `cdr` and "
"`almax`. Cache entries are isolated by `(method, linelist_hash, stellar "
"params)`, so one folder can safely store multiple linelists and both "
"methods together. Legacy `cdr_database` is still accepted as an alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:55
msgid "ALMAX strong-line rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:57
msgid "`line_select_almax_use_bins=False`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:58
msgid "`strong = (almax_ratio >= line_select_almax_threshold)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:59
msgid "`line_select_almax_use_bins=True`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:60
msgid ""
"`strong = flag_strong_lines_by_bins(wl, almax_ratio, "
"threshold=line_select_almax_threshold, "
"bin_width=line_select_almax_bin_width)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/line_filtering.md:62
msgid ""
"`line_select_almax_threshold` is the single ALMAX threshold parameter for"
" both rules. If it is `None`, it falls back to `sme.accrt` (legacy-"
"compatible behavior)."
msgstr ""

